`emit` is `const`, so `handlers_[event]` does not compile (it could insert). Look the event up with `find` and bail out when it is missing.
```cpp
auto it = handlers_.find(event);
if (it == handlers_.end()) return 0;
```

Then call every handler in order and report how many there were. `clear` is just `handlers_.erase(event);` (erasing a missing key is a no-op).
```cpp
for (const auto& h : it->second) h(payload);
return it->second.size();
```
